  "version": "enrolled",
  "operative_text": "(a_in_person_id) not stated.\n(b_no_id_remedy) not stated.\n(c_mail_ballot_id) not stated.\n(d_proof_of_citizenship) not stated.\n(e_other_rule) not stated.\n(other) 3501.055 (new): election integrity unit in the secretary of state's office; investigates alleged Title 35 violations, takes public allegations, reports yearly, may subpoena; prosecutors must act on its referrals within one year or explain.\n(other) 3501.05(N): secretary of state investigates election fraud through the new unit; receives complaints for the Ohio election integrity commission.\n(other) 3517.13-3517.23 (changed): Ohio Elections Commission replaced by an Ohio Election Integrity Commission in the secretary of state's office (five members, chair chosen by the secretary of state); complaint and penalty references updated; 3517.991 (new) says violators are sentenced under the law in force when the act occurred.\n(other) 3501.01, 3501.02, 3505.03, 3505.04, 3505.06, 3505.33, 3505.38, 3513.04, 3513.05, 3513.052, 3513.19, 3517.092-3517.109: strike \"member of the state board of education\" wording from election sections; 3501.02 changes petition day counts and a date reference.\n(other) 3501.12, 3501.17: board of elections member pay increases; who pays for certain local option elections.\n(other) 3517.1012: lists allowed uses of state party funds.\n(other) Rest of the budget (thousands of pages) is not election law and was not read.\n(other) version: 00_IN, 01_RH, 02_PH, 03_PSC, 04_RS, 05_PS, 06_CR: text file not saved, not read. 07_EN (enrolled, read for election sections): no ID or citizenship text in slots a-d.\n(other) note: State operating budget; only the enrolled text (07_EN, 9.7 MB) was saved, so earlier versions were not read. Searched all of R.C. Title 35 changes, BMV sections (4501-4507) and 3503/3505/3509 text: no photo ID, mail-ballot ID, proof-of-citizenship or citizenship-check text. 3501.01 reprints the existing photo-ID definition and the noncitizen-license wording unchanged. The last two votes (2025-07-21, 2025-10-01) were on overriding line-item vetoes; which items they covered is not in the saved text.\n(note) Off this topic: the bill sets no ID or citizenship-proof rule.",
